  "caveats": [
    "libero_10's D_lib library source is NOT the historical 2026-04-21 corpus. That corpus's H5 carry no init identity in their attrs and its init map has only 5 fields, so the content-level census required by this line cannot be satisfied without inference -- exactly what the census exists to reject. The 5 official inits per task were therefore read out of the historical map (preserving the historical D_lib choice) and re-collected on 2026-08-28 via exp/dispatch_surface/bootstrap_library_source.py, which then rebuilds a complete init map from the fresh H5 attrs and re-runs the census as a self-check.",
    "The partition is only meaningful together with its seed and the init map: re-running split_init_pools with a different seed produces a different, equally valid partition, and any artifact calibrated on the old one no longer matches.",
    "test_aprime is the precheck A' pool and must never be read by calibration or fitting; query_c is the fit/cal cohort pool and must never be evaluated on. The split manifest is what downstream scripts bind to for that separation."
  ],
  "consumers": [
    "exp/dispatch_surface/rebuild_dispatch_library.py (re-verifies the D_lib census)",
    "exp/dispatch_surface/collect_query_cohort.py (rolls out query_c)",
    "exp/dispatch_surface/build_dispatch_table.py (fit/cal split assignment)",
    "exp/dispatch_surface/run_precheck.py (test_aprime)"
  ],
